    {
      "what": "five-mile road once connected Griffith to Merrillville, closed since the 1970s; shadow figure sometimes holding a lantern by the train tracks; Elizabeth Wilson story is the vanishing-hitchhiker kind; no burial records of an Elizabeth Wilson found in Ross Cemetery",
      "who": "Ghost Research Society (Dale Kaczmarek), Reder Road Investigation",
      "url": "https://ghostresearch.org/Investigations/reder.html"
    },
    {
      "what": "five-mile road between Griffith and Merrillville; yellow barricades; a man in black walking toward you from the tracks at night",
      "who": "Occult World, 'Reeder Road - Griffith' (Sharon Blumberg)",
      "url": "https://occult-world.com/?p=81322"
    },
    {
      "what": "legend: Elizabeth Wilson drowned in a swamp when her car went off the road; she waits for a ride and disappears at Ross Cemetery, where she was buried in 1955",
      "who": "HauntedPlaces.org, Reder Road",
      "url": "https://hauntedplaces.org/?p=51736"
    },
    {
      "what": "legend (per Indiana Haunted Houses): in the 1950s a young woman crashed on Reeder Road and drowned in a nearby swamp; her ghost is seen walking down the road hoping for a ride",
